assistant: Subject: read unit_amount when price is missing
Vendor API 2026-10-01 renamed the product field `price` to `unit_amount` without updating its spec. `get_product` only read `p.price`, so on the new version `?? null` turned every price into null with no error. The handler now reads `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`, so responses from the old version (which have `price`) give exactly the same output as before. I assumed `unit_amount` is in dollars like `price` was, not cents. The only evidence is one product: p-1001 has `price: 1199` in the old recording and `unit_amount: 1199` in the new one, and it's the only `unit_amount` value anywhere in the tests. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass, including the repro test. `search_products` and `get_order` still read the old price field names; I didn't check whether the new version renamed those too.

